# Docs browser (`DOCS_ACCESS`)

| Mode | Public | Login required |
|------|--------|----------------|
| `protected` (default) | `/`, `/docs/md/*`, assets | `/docs/api`, `/docs/model/*`, `/model*`, `/docs/account/*` |
| `disabled` | same | model explorer → 404 |
| `public` | all | none |

Sign-in page (`/docs/login`) calls `POST /docs/session` with email/password and receives an HttpOnly session cookie plus a short-lived console key. The console key is kept in sessionStorage and revoked on logout. The session endpoint uses login rate limiting (`login_rate_limit.ts`); handle HTTP 429 in `docs-login.js`.

## Restify

- Sync middleware: `(req, res, next)` + `res.redirect(302, url, next)`
- Async routes: `(req, res)` + `sendRedirect(res, url)` for redirects

## Tests

Run `npm run test` after changes. See `test/docs_auth.test.js`.
